    "viz_hunt_intro": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# HUNT — guided investigation\n\nTwo paths. Path A is the default. Path B is an answer key, not a replacement.\n\n**Path A — Try it yourself:** question, starter guidance, [Open Splunk Search](/en-US/app/search/search). Construct the hunt.\n\n**Path B — Show solution (optional):** copyable SPL from existing Q-MCP hunts, bound REPLAY table, explanation, limitations. Open it only after Path A. It is an answer key, not policy.\n\nEvidence to investigate is canonical **REPLAY**. Fresh LIVE run.id comes from Attack Service Search handoff. Studio tokens are not auto-bound.\n\nDo not search until Attack Service reports **EVIDENCE READY** (or you have measured searchable events). HEC success is not ready.\n\nThis tab is a **stacked notebook**: Path A, then optional hints, then Path B. Custom browser scripts are not used.\n\nALLOW is the control decision. Runtime handler count is authoritative for execution. Indexed `mcp.started` (`executed=true` on that event) corroborates that the handler began on a complete copy. Do not read ALLOW as execution. `mcp.completed` is success of a begun call. `mcp.failed` is execution then error, not prevention.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "STEP 4 HUNT"
    },
    "viz_i1_q": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Investigation 1 — Find the run\n\n**QUESTION**\n\nCan you reconstruct the events that belong to this experiment?\n\n**WHAT AM I TRYING TO PROVE?**\n\nUse run.id as the forensic correlation key. One UUID, one experiment copy.\n\n**YOUR TASK (Path A — try it yourself)**\n\nIndex agentsec_telemetry, sourcetype otel:agentic:json. Filter quoted agentsec.run.id. Do not search index=*. Then name the principal, agent, and tool.\n\n1. Copy your LIVE run.id from the Attack Service Workbench, or use a recorded REPLAY example from the INVESTIGATE tab.\n2. [Open Splunk Search](/en-US/app/search/search)\n3. Constrain `index=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json`.\n4. Filter quoted `agentsec.run.id`. Execute. Read the fields yourself.\n\nThe Workbench's **Investigate evidence** link fills the LIVE box on the INVESTIGATE tab for you. Splunk Search is a separate app, so here you enter the run.id yourself.\n\nStarter (paste your LIVE run.id; do not search `index=*`):\n\n```\nindex=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json earliest=0 \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"PASTE-LIVE-RUN-ID\"\n```\n\nNeed help? Scroll to **Hint 1**, then **Hint 2**, then the Path B solution. Do not skip Path A.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I1 question"
    },
    "viz_i1_h1": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# HINT 1 — Investigation 1\n\nStart with index=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json and the quoted field agentsec.run.id. Paste the LIVE run.id from Attack Service, or use the Investigate specimen REPLAY id.\n\nPath A is still Search. This is not the full solution.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I1 hint 1"
    },
    "viz_i1_h2": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# HINT 2 — Investigation 1\n\nQ-MCP-WHO is the governed hunt for principal / agent / tool on control.decision. Count physical events with stats dc(_raw) as n. Do not use stats count by agentsec.run.id.\n\nPath A is still Search. This is not the full solution.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I1 hint 2"
    },
    "viz_i1_sol": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Solution — Investigation 1 Find the run\n\nThis is **Path B — show solution**. Open it only after you tried Path A in Search. It is an answer key, not policy. Splunk does not enforce. Path A remains Search with your LIVE run.id.\n\n**SOLUTION SPL** (`Q-MCP-WHO`)\n\nCopy this into Search. Replace `$run_id$` with the LIVE UUID, or leave the token for Evidence to investigate REPLAY.\n\n```\nindex=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json earliest=0 \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"$run_id$\" \"event.name\"=agentsec.control.decision\n| eval run_id=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.run.id'),0)\n| eval principal=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.principal.id'),0)\n| eval agent=mvindex(mvdedup('gen_ai.agent.id'),0)\n| eval tool=mvindex(mvdedup('gen_ai.tool.name'),0)\n| eval method=mvindex(mvdedup('mcp.method.name'),0)\n| eval profile=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.security.profile'),0)\n| eval mode=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.testbed.mode'),0)\n| table run_id, principal, agent, tool, method, profile, mode\n```\n\n**WHY THESE STAGES**\n\n- **Why control.decision?** Identity of who requested which tool is on the authorization event.\n- **Why not session.id?** AgentSec correlates with run.id.\n- **Why collapse mvindex(mvdedup(...),0)?** JSON body and OTLP attributes duplicate scalars.\n\n**EXPECTED RESULT SHAPE**\n\nOne control.decision identity row per run. LIVE ATTACK (vulnerable) and BASELINE also have mcp.* rows in the copy. Defended RETEST has control.decision and no mcp.started. Canonical REPLAY schema on this volume may be 1.1.0; fresh LIVE after restage is 1.9.0.\n\n**WHAT YOU ARE SEEING**\n\nYou are looking at the indexed copy of one MCP invoke. run.id is the experiment key. tool is what was requested, not what was granted.\n\n**WHAT IT MEANS**\n\nCorrelation starts with run.id. Without it you mix experiments. Rows in Splunk are a copy of telemetry, not an authorization decision.\n\n**WHAT IT DOES NOT MEAN**\n\nIndex presence does not prove completeness, prevention, or that the handler ran. Empty is not SAFE.\n\n**SECURITY CONNECTION**\n\nControl `none on this step — you are locating evidence, not judging CTRL-MCP-001 yet` · invariant `INV-007` · hunt `Q-MCP-WHO`. Splunk does **not** ALLOW or DENY.\n\n**NEXT CHALLENGE**\n\nMCP-I2-FIND-THE-REQUEST\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I1 solution"
    },
    "viz_i1_tbl": {
      "type": "splunk.table",
      "title": "Q-MCP-WHO (REPLAY specimen)",
      "description": "Path B identity row. Fresh LIVE run.id is Search, not this table.",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_q_who"
      },
      "showProgressBar": true,
