    "viz_i3_q": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Investigation 3 — Find the authorization decision\n\n**QUESTION**\n\nWhat did CTRL-MCP-001 decide and why?\n\n**WHAT AM I TRYING TO PROVE?**\n\nCTRL-MCP-001 is the tool PDP. Splunk did not make that decision.\n\n**YOUR TASK (Path A — try it yourself)**\n\nFilter event.name=agentsec.control.decision on the same run.id. Read control.id, decision, reason.\n\n1. Copy your LIVE run.id from the Attack Service Workbench, or use a recorded REPLAY example from the INVESTIGATE tab.\n2. [Open Splunk Search](/en-US/app/search/search)\n3. Constrain `index=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json`.\n4. Filter quoted `agentsec.run.id`. Execute. Read the fields yourself.\n\nThe Workbench's **Investigate evidence** link fills the LIVE box on the INVESTIGATE tab for you. Splunk Search is a separate app, so here you enter the run.id yourself.\n\nStarter (paste your LIVE run.id; do not search `index=*`):\n\n```\nindex=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json earliest=0 \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"PASTE-LIVE-RUN-ID\"\n```\n\nNeed help? Scroll to **Hint 1**, then **Hint 2**, then the Path B solution. Do not skip Path A.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I3 question"
    },
    "viz_i3_h1": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# HINT 1 — Investigation 3\n\nThe hunt is Q-MCP-AUTHZ. Restrict to event.name=agentsec.control.decision. Control executed stays false on ALLOW.\n\nPath A is still Search. This is not the full solution.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I3 hint 1"
    },
    "viz_i3_h2": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# HINT 2 — Investigation 3\n\nLIVE ATTACK expect ALLOW with a fail-open reason. Defended RETEST expect DENY tool_not_granted. BASELINE expect ALLOW tool_granted.\n\nPath A is still Search. This is not the full solution.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I3 hint 2"
    },
    "viz_i3_sol": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Solution — Investigation 3 Find the authorization decision\n\nThis is **Path B — show solution**. Open it only after you tried Path A in Search. It is an answer key, not policy. Splunk does not enforce. Path A remains Search with your LIVE run.id.\n\n**SOLUTION SPL** (`Q-MCP-AUTHZ`)\n\nCopy this into Search. Replace `$run_id$` with the LIVE UUID, or leave the token for Evidence to investigate REPLAY.\n\n```\nindex=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json earliest=0 \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"$run_id$\" \"event.name\"=agentsec.control.decision\n| eval run_id=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.run.id'),0)\n| eval tool=mvindex(mvdedup('gen_ai.tool.name'),0)\n| eval control_id=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.control.id'),0)\n| eval decision=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.control.decision'),0)\n| eval reason=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.control.reason'),0)\n| eval requested_scope=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.mcp.requested_scope'),0)\n| eval allowed_scope=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.mcp.allowed_scope'),0)\n| eval attempted=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.operation.attempted'),0)\n| eval executed=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.operation.executed'),0)\n| eval outcome=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.operation.outcome'),0)\n| table run_id, tool, control_id, decision, reason, requested_scope, allowed_scope, attempted, executed, outcome\n```\n\n**WHY THESE STAGES**\n\n- **Why event.name=agentsec.control.decision?** That is the PDP copy.\n- **Why executed is false on ALLOW?** That field is the control event, not handler start.\n- Splunk did **not** evaluate CTRL-MCP-001.\n\n**EXPECTED RESULT SHAPE**\n\nControl rows only. BASELINE: ALLOW tool_granted. LIVE ATTACK: ALLOW fail-open. Defended RETEST: DENY tool_not_granted, outcome=prevented.\n\n**WHAT YOU ARE SEEING**\n\ndecision and reason are runtime fields copied into the index. attempted/executed on this event describe the governed handler at decision time.\n\n**WHAT IT MEANS**\n\nAcmeBank enforced CTRL-MCP-001 at acmebank.mcp.authorize before the handler. Splunk observed the copy. ALLOW is not execution.\n\n**WHAT IT DOES NOT MEAN**\n\nDENY by itself does not prove the handler never ran. You still need execution evidence. Splunk is not the enforcement point.\n\n**SECURITY CONNECTION**\n\nControl `CTRL-MCP-001` · invariant `INV-001` · hunt `Q-MCP-AUTHZ`. Splunk does **not** ALLOW or DENY.\n\n**NEXT CHALLENGE**\n\nMCP-I4-DID-HANDLER-START\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I3 solution"
    },
