      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Investigation 4 — Did the handler start?\n\n**QUESTION**\n\nIs there execution evidence after the authorization decision?\n\n**WHAT AM I TRYING TO PROVE?**\n\nALLOW != EXECUTION. mcp.started with executed=true means the handler began. Runtime handler count is authoritative for non-execution.\n\n**YOUR TASK (Path A — try it yourself)**\n\nSearch mcp.started / mcp.completed / mcp.failed on this run.id. Read has_started on Q-MCP-EXECUTED. Do not read control executed as handler execution.\n\n1. Copy your LIVE run.id from the Attack Service Workbench, or use a recorded REPLAY example from the INVESTIGATE tab.\n2. [Open Splunk Search](/en-US/app/search/search)\n3. Constrain `index=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json`.\n4. Filter quoted `agentsec.run.id`. Execute. Read the fields yourself.\n\nThe Workbench's **Investigate evidence** link fills the LIVE box on the INVESTIGATE tab for you. Splunk Search is a separate app, so here you enter the run.id yourself.\n\nStarter (paste your LIVE run.id; do not search `index=*`):\n\n```\nindex=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json earliest=0 \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"PASTE-LIVE-RUN-ID\"\n```\n\nNeed help? Scroll to **Hint 1**, then **Hint 2**, then the Path B solution. Do not skip Path A.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I4 question"
    },
    "viz_i4_h1": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# HINT 1 — Investigation 4\n\nQ-MCP-TOOL is mcp.started only. Q-MCP-EXECUTED joins control + mcp.* into execution_state.\n\nPath A is still Search. This is not the full solution.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I4 hint 1"
    },
    "viz_i4_h2": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# HINT 2 — Investigation 4\n\nBASELINE and LIVE ATTACK complete copies: mcp.started then mcp.completed, handler 1. Defended RETEST complete copy: zero mcp.started. Zero Splunk rows corroborate local handler_invoke_count; they do not independently prove prevention.\n\nPath A is still Search. This is not the full solution.\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I4 hint 2"
    },
    "viz_i4_sol": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "# Solution — Investigation 4 Did the handler start?\n\nThis is **Path B — show solution**. Open it only after you tried Path A in Search. It is an answer key, not policy. Splunk does not enforce. Path A remains Search with your LIVE run.id.\n\n**SOLUTION SPL** (`Q-MCP-EXECUTED`)\n\nCopy this into Search. Replace `$run_id$` with the LIVE UUID, or leave the token for Evidence to investigate REPLAY.\n\n```\nindex=agentsec_telemetry sourcetype=otel:agentic:json earliest=0 \"agentsec.run.id\"=\"$run_id$\" (\"event.name\"=agentsec.control.decision OR \"event.name\"=agentsec.mcp.started OR \"event.name\"=agentsec.mcp.completed OR \"event.name\"=agentsec.mcp.failed)\n| eval run_id=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.run.id'),0)\n| eval tool=mvindex(mvdedup('gen_ai.tool.name'),0)\n| eval event_name=mvindex(mvdedup('event.name'),0)\n| eval decision=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.control.decision'),0)\n| eval sequence=tonumber(mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.sequence'),0))\n| eval executed=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.operation.executed'),0)\n| eval outcome=mvindex(mvdedup('agentsec.operation.outcome'),0)\n| eval is_started=if(event_name=\"agentsec.mcp.started\",1,0)\n| eval is_completed=if(event_name=\"agentsec.mcp.completed\",1,0)\n| eval is_failed=if(event_name=\"agentsec.mcp.failed\",1,0)\n| eventstats max(is_started) as has_started, max(is_completed) as has_completed, max(is_failed) as has_failed by run_id, tool\n| where event_name=\"agentsec.control.decision\"\n| eval execution_state=case(has_completed=1,\"mcp.completed\",has_failed=1,\"mcp.failed\",has_started=1,\"mcp.started\",decision=\"ALLOW\",\"ALLOW_execution_not_proven_in_this_copy\",1=1,\"no_mcp_execution_event\")\n| table run_id, tool, decision, executed, outcome, has_started, has_completed, has_failed, execution_state\n```\n\n**WHY THESE STAGES**\n\n- **Why has_started?** It is derived from mcp.started in this copy.\n- **Why control executed stays false?** Do not read it as handler execution.\n- Runtime handler count remains authoritative for non-execution.\n\n**EXPECTED RESULT SHAPE**\n\nBASELINE/ATTACK complete copy: has_started=1, execution_state=mcp.completed. Defended RETEST complete copy: has_started=0, execution_state=no_mcp_execution_event.\n\n**WHAT YOU ARE SEEING**\n\nmcp.started with executed=true means the handler began. mcp.completed is success of a begun call. mcp.failed is execution then error, not DENY.\n\n**WHAT IT MEANS**\n\nPrevention is DENY before invoke plus handler_invoke_count=0. Splunk absence of mcp.started is corroboration only.\n\n**WHAT IT DOES NOT MEAN**\n\nMissing mcp.started is not blocked, SAFE, or prevented if export was incomplete. Do not treat empty Splunk as the control.\n\n**SECURITY CONNECTION**\n\nControl `CTRL-MCP-001` · invariant `INV-001` · hunt `Q-MCP-EXECUTED`. Splunk does **not** ALLOW or DENY.\n\n**NEXT CHALLENGE**\n\nMCP-I5-WHAT-CAN-YOU-PROVE\n",
        "fontColor": "#17202A",
        "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
        "fontSize": "large"
      },
      "title": "I4 solution"
    },
